  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Every new member receives the same brief introduction before independent work; a steward, experienced member, or illustrated guide can support it.\", \"decision\": \"How should a new member learn the studio routine?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe steward walks each new member through the illustrated guide before their first session. A short conversation connects the written routine to the places and equipment the member will actually use.\nAn experienced member accompanies each new member through the illustrated guide at the start of their first session. A peer demonstrates the routine and remains an approachable contact during the first project.\nNew members follow the illustrated guide through the studio and then explain the routine to the steward. The steward checks understanding after members have explored the space at their own pace."
    }
  ],
